Z||000000||mlmpetert||07-23-2001||09:25 PM||||i have a 86 fiero gt and i just changed the spark plug wires and in the process the battery went dead ( had to go to the store 4 times to get the right plugs and i kept the interior lights and trunk lights on the whole time) and now when i put the keys in the ignition it make the normal beeping when the keys are in but then it makes a very fast paced beeping about 4 seconds after. It continuies this when i start the car. Any ideas? thanks Peter ||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||07-23-2001||09:48 PM||||That is the e-brake 'dinger'.  Put the brake on then put it back down and that should turn it off. If it comes back on w/o you touching the handle, then you may need to adjust the switch (a PITA). GL||||reg||1
